@startuml sd_us228
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
title US228 - Sequence Diagram
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
actor "Backoffice Operator" as Actor
participant "Entry (Envoy)\nvirtual IP of airports-routes" as EAR
box "airports-routes-n (the replica that answers)" #F7F7F7
participant "RouteController" as RouteController
participant "ExportRouteNetworkUseCase" as ExportRouteNetworkUseCase
database "own database" as DBAR
end box
collections "peer replicas\nairports-routes-m" as PAR
== GET /api/routes/export?format={geojson|kml} ==
Actor -> EAR : GET /api/routes/export?format={geojson|kml}\n(HTTPS, Authorization: Bearer JWT)
EAR -> RouteController : to a ready replica\n(another one if it fails)
RouteController -> ExportRouteNetworkUseCase : execute(...)
ExportRouteNetworkUseCase -> DBAR : own routes
ExportRouteNetworkUseCase -> PAR : GET /internal/replicas/routes\n(every peer in parallel)
PAR --> ExportRouteNetworkUseCase : their routes
ExportRouteNetworkUseCase -> DBAR : airports (catalog, complete here)
ExportRouteNetworkUseCase -> ExportRouteNetworkUseCase : keep the latest change of each record,\nleave out deleted ones; filter, compute, sort, page
ExportRouteNetworkUseCase --> RouteController : result
RouteController --> Actor : 200 OK (X-Node-Id; X-Partial-Result if both holders of a record were unreachable)
@enduml
